<title>ITALY: Olivetti suspended again after brief open.</title>
<headline>Olivetti suspended again after brief open.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Olivetti were suspended again on the Milan bourse after briefly re-opening down 9.93 percent at 516 lire, but soon moved to touch a new record low of 515 lire.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended automatically on the Milan stock exchange earlier on Monday when they touched a 10 percent fluctuation limit.</p>
<p>Trading in the stock is hoped to start at 1236 GMT, the stock market council said.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
